From 134093194a4754f3e67fe6eb2b9df80a2061987c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carter Blair <cartergblair@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 18:38:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat: route matching diagnostics through Cloud Logging
 instead of the response

Adopts the logger from #6 across the absolute-diversity text matching path.

Response now carries only what the client renders: groupId, participantIds,
diversityLevel, diffusionStatement. Moved to structured extra_data:

- assignedTarget, achievedDiversity, fallbackUsed
- participantResponses, which was the largest item in the payload on a big
  event and is diagnostic rather than actionable for the client
- the pool geometry targets were derived from: pool mean, achievable floor and
  ceiling per group size, and r_star_by_size

r_star = (ceiling * margin - mean) / (mean - floor) is the ratio at which the
achievable ceiling starts binding, so low groups past it buy no additional
contrast. LOW_TO_HIGH_RATIO is currently 2.5 against a measured r_star of
roughly 0.26-0.49 on synthetic pools; logging it per event is what allows the
constant to be set from real data.

Also:
- group-size report per request (planned vs actual, histogram, assignment
  coverage); mismatch logs WARNING, unassigned participants log ERROR
- condition_counts keyed on diversity_level, since raw targets are continuous
- WARNING when the high arm has fewer than two groups, where the contrast is
  not estimable
- thread the FastAPI request through TextMatchingService.match so matching logs
  share the request trace
- fix embedding_client.py calling an unimported Log class with a missing
  request argument
- one aggregate participant-response log instead of one call per participant
- openapi.yaml, README and demo updated for the trimmed contract
