From 7fa07f2a9af3d329b7fc75d6080a02f144e6bc7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carter Blair <cartergblair@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:32:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat: REQUIRE_REAL_TEXT strict mode refuses placeholder
 substitution

Groups formed from placeholder text achieve their diversity targets perfectly
and demonstrate nothing about the participants. At a one-shot live event that
failure is silent and unrecoverable. With REQUIRE_REAL_TEXT=1 the API instead
returns 422 MISSING_TEXT_RESPONSES listing the affected participant ids, so a
broken survey pipeline is caught at the pre-event dry run instead of after
matching.
