From 5dc83496fe58f7daaa315c0ea5f538b999bcb32a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carter Blair <cartergblair@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:38:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat: allocate arms sqrt(2):1:1 for the curvature
 contrast

The confirmatory analysis is now the curvature contrast 2M - L - H (interior
optimum), with the linear contrast H - L registered separately. sqrt(2):1:1
minimises the larger marginal variance of the medium-versus-extreme
comparisons and sits within a few percent of the variance-minimising
allocation for the curvature contrast, while keeping the extreme arms large
enough to keep the linear contrast informative: 6/8/6 at 20 groups, 7/11/7 at
25, matching the reviewed design note.

Extreme arms are held equal so that sum(c1_i * c2_i / n_i) == 0 for the linear
and quadratic contrasts -- the two registered hypotheses are then exactly
orthogonal and neither borrows evidence from the other.
