From 6324e64adf004072f1e484cb2c94e11e14f0dda8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carter Blair <cartergblair@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 01:00:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] docs: state the arm-allocation trade-off honestly

The sqrt(2):1:1 allocation does not follow from the curvature contrast being
primary -- that contrast alone is minimised by 2:1:1 (5/10/5 at 20 groups).
sqrt(2):1:1 is a compromise across the three quantities the analysis plan
commits to, and it costs the primary about 1.7 points of power to gain about
5.3 on the linear contrast. Record the numbers rather than implying a single
optimum.
